{"benchmark": "ifeval", "task_id": "1082", "sample_idx": 42, "model_name": "google/gemma-3n-e2b-it", "content": "The sunlight felt…different. Sharper. Brighter, but somehow *programmed*. Arthur blinked, the familiar floral wallpaper of his bedroom resolving into a pixelated grid. His hand instinctively reached for his glasses, but the lenses shimmered with a strange, internal glow. He looked down at his hands – perfectly sculpted, with impossibly smooth skin and nails that gleamed with an unnatural clarity. A wave of nausea washed over him, not from illness, but from a profound sense of wrongness. He tried to sit up, and his limbs felt…responsive, almost too perfect. A faint, digital hum resonated from the walls, a subtle backdrop to the unnerving quiet of his room. He glanced at the digital clock on his nightstand; 6:00 AM. It felt…unnatural.\n\nArthur stumbled out of bed, his movements strangely fluid and precise. The floor wasn't wood, but a perfectly rendered tile, each one gleaming with a simulated sheen. He peered out the window, and the view wasn’t his familiar suburban street. Instead, a vibrant, fantastical landscape unfolded – rolling green hills dotted with quaint, cobblestone villages, a crystal-clear river snaking through the valley, and a sky painted with hues he’d only seen in graphics editors. A notification popped up in his vision: \"Character Name: Arthur. Level: 1. Quest: Wake up.\" He stared, dumbfounded, at the words. This wasn't his life. This wasn't real. He was trapped, somehow, inside a video game.\n\n\n\n***", "logprobs": [{"token": "The", "logprob": -0.6729406118392944}, {"token": "▁sunlight", "logprob": -0.9427294135093689}, {"token": "▁felt", "logprob": -0.1230592280626297}, {"token": "…", "logprob": -0.02061885967850685}, {"token": "different", "logprob": -0.7912519574165344}, {"token": ".", "logprob": -2.8371408916427754e-05}, {"token": "▁Shar", "logprob": -0.7341781854629517}, {"token": "per", "logprob": -3.099436753473128e-06}, {"tok